{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3954","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3954","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3954\",\"parent_revision\":\"2cbc556ab73fadcbda20f7689fb12c6a27b58d0d\",\"root_revision\":\"865ce3b7851c4b868e567a5771ff1799b39dd861255f3332d56b503b2c68f729\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: needs-grooming\\nadded: 2026-09-26\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/development-harness/scripts/verify_migration_fidelity.py` compares a legacy `.md.bak` backlog item with its migrated `.yaml` item. It reports `CONTENT_GAIN` for every faithful pair. The cause is the `## Sections` index block that the rendered body carries and the legacy body does not. The description is not the cause.\\n\\nThe test suite does not catch this. The fixture at `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_verify_migration_fidelity.py:78` builds the expected `.md.bak` body with `render_sections_as_body`, which is the same function whose output the script checks. The oracle is therefore not independent of the code under test, so the test and the script agree on the same mistake.\\n\\nObserved by the agent that fixed the PR #3951 review findings. The behaviour is pre-existing on `origin/main` and is out of scope for #3951.\\n\\nImpact: a migration fidelity check that flags every correct migration gives no signal. An operator either learns to ignore CONTENT_GAIN, which hides a real content gain, or investigates false positives.\\n\\nOpen question for grooming: which side defines fidelity \u2014 the legacy body's shape, or the rendered body's shape \u2014 and whether the index block counts as content.\\n\\nRelated: finding 2 of the #3951 review noted that an item with both a frontmatter description and an `unknown__description` section also produced a spurious CONTENT_GAIN in this script (`verify_migration_fidelity.py:379`). #3951 fixes that source. The index-block source remains.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Found during code-review follow-up on PR #3951\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-26\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e0acffb28e791297d591214af9d2fc12fcdee77d76e0c5e2417b1ed2df5e8525\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABYnIYqg\",\"fields\":{\"followup_to\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"added\":\"2026-09-26\",\"layer\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\",\"source\":\"Not specified\",\"priority\":\"P2\",\"language\":\"\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"status\":\"needs-grooming\",\"close_reason\":\"\",\"stack\":\"\",\"item_type\":\"Bug\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"files\":\"\",\"topic\":\"\",\"groomed\":\"\",\"plan\":\"\"}}"}